sxml-xslt-test list - List test cases with their stylesheets, plans and applicability

Usage: sxml-xslt-test list [--catalog=FILE] [--test-set=NAME] [TEST-LIST]

Reads the XSLT 4.0 catalog with sxml's XML parser and writes each
selected test case: its environment (sources, stylesheets,
packages, parameters, resources, collections), the stylesheets
and parameters of its test, how it invokes the stylesheet, its
output and dependencies, the plan of its transformation, the
kinds of its assertions, and, when it cannot run for XSLT 4.0,
"skip:" and the reason; "out of scope:" when it is outside the
D95 denominator. The last line counts the test cases, those that
run, and those in scope. The selection is the test cases of
TEST-LIST, those of the test set --test-set names, or with neither
every test case of the catalog. Exits 1 when a test set, test
case or environment does not exist or a test case is malformed, 3
when a file cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --catalog=FILE   The catalog.xml of the suite (default: third_party/xslt40-test/catalog.xml)
      --test-set=NAME  Select every test case of one test set

Arguments:
  TEST-LIST  File naming test cases, one '<test-set> <test-case>' per line

Examples:
  sxml-xslt-test list tests/xslt/slice.txt
  sxml-xslt-test list --test-set=apply-templates
